# ==========================================================================
#  Q84  CONSTRUCT WHERE, the short form
# ==========================================================================
#
#  ASKS
#    Extract the shops with their names and founding years, unchanged.
#
#  HOW IT WORKS
#    When the template you want is exactly the pattern you matched, the
#    template can be omitted. `CONSTRUCT WHERE { ... }` uses the pattern as
#    its own template. It's the standard way to cut a subgraph out of a
#    larger one without retyping it.
#
#  DIAGRAM
#        the long way:
#
#          CONSTRUCT { ?shop a bs:Bookshop ; rdfs:label ?n ; bs:founded ?y }
#          WHERE     { ?shop a bs:Bookshop ; rdfs:label ?n ; bs:founded ?y }
#                      --------------- identical ---------------
#
#        the short way:
#
#          CONSTRUCT WHERE { ?shop a bs:Bookshop ; rdfs:label ?n ; bs:founded ?y }
#
#        99 triples out: three per shop.
#
#        Restrictions, and the reason they exist -- the pattern IS the
#        template, so it must be something a template could contain:
#
#          no FILTER, no OPTIONAL, no UNION, no sub-query
#          just a basic graph pattern
#
#        Need any of those?  Write the template out.  That is q85.
#
#
#  WHAT TO TAKE AWAY
#    - CONSTRUCT WHERE { ... } reuses the pattern as the template, and is
#      the idiomatic way to extract a subgraph unchanged.
#    - It accepts only a basic graph pattern: no FILTER, OPTIONAL, UNION
#      or sub-query.
#    - The moment you need to reshape anything, write the template out in
#      full.
#
#  DATA     bookshop-trail-1.1.ttl
#  LOAD IT  https://semantechs.co.uk/turtle-editor-viewer/?dot=https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fpwin%2FSPARQL_Course%2Fmain%2Fdata%2Fbookshop-trail-1.1.ttl
#  RUNS ON  editor, holos, fuseki
#  SPEC     SPARQL 1.2 Query 16.2 CONSTRUCT
#           https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql12-query/#x16-2-construct
#           SPARQL 1.2 Query 16.2.1 Templates with Blank Nodes
#           https://www.w3.org/TR/sparql12-query/#x16-2-1-templates-with-blank-nodes
#  RETURNS  99 rows, on every engine that runs it
# ==========================================================================

PREFIX bt:   <https://example.org/bookshop-trail/>
PREFIX bs:   <https://example.org/bookshop-trail/schema#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

CONSTRUCT WHERE {
  ?shop a          bs:Bookshop ;
        rdfs:label ?name ;
        bs:founded ?year .
}
